193 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 194 0 R/Alt(A schematic drawing. A long gray beam, labeled "test article (flexible)" beneath it, rests on three blue hatched shakers drawn as boxes with an armature on top, labeled shaker 1, shaker 2 and shaker 3. Three orange triangles on the beam mark control accelerometers, labeled control 1 to 3, and one open green triangle between control 1 and control 2 marks a limit accelerometer. A dashed outline of the beam bent in its first mode shape is drawn over it. On the right a box labeled "controller" contains three smaller boxes in a row: "tracking filters: amplitude and phase of each channel at the tone", "compare with the reference R (amplitude and phase at each control)", and "update the drives D". Dotted orange arrows run from each control accelerometer and from the limit accelerometer to the tracking filters box; solid blue arrows run from the drive box back to each shaker, labeled d1, d2 and d3. A note under the controller reads "C = H D at each frequency: H is measured before the test".)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[13]/Pg 991 0 R>>
endobj
